## 5. Data model in simple terms

The database is relational and tracks real-world relationships.

- User
  - identity and authentication information
- Category
  - expense label such as Food, Travel, Groceries, Health
- Transaction
  - merchant, date, amount, category, user
- Receipt
  - uploaded image metadata and OCR/parsed output
- Forecast / ML output
  - predicted spending or anomaly summary

The important relationship is:

User -> many Transactions
Category -> many Transactions
Transaction -> belongs to one user and one category

That structure allows reporting by user, category, and time period.

