## 6. Frontend state pattern

The frontend uses Zustand stores instead of a massive app-wide context tree.

Examples:

- authStore.js: stores login state and token info
- categoryStore.js: loads and manages categories
- transactionStore.js: list and create transactions
- forecastStore.js: stores forecast data
- themeStore.js: handles dark mode state
- toastStore.js: common user notifications

This keeps the UI modular: screens request only what they need, and the stores control the data lifecycle.

---

## 7. Dark mode behavior

Dark mode is implemented with Tailwind’s dark variants.

- The app checks a theme store state like isDark
- Components use classes such as dark:bg-white/5, dark:text-white, dark:border-white/10
- The selected theme toggles the color system without rewriting the entire UI

This is why light/dark styling is consistent across pages with minimal custom CSS.

