## 8. How the whole project fits together

The simplest “thin-thread” summary is:

User interacts with frontend -> frontend sends request to API -> backend validates and reads/writes database -> background tasks process heavy work -> frontend displays analytics and results

Example end-to-end flow for a new transaction:

1. User goes to Add Transaction
2. Selects category and enters amount
3. Frontend sends payload to backend
4. Backend validates request
5. SQLAlchemy saves record to PostgreSQL
6. Dashboard fetches updated list
7. Charts recalculate totals
8. User sees updated spending summary instantly

For a receipt upload:

1. User uploads image
2. Frontend sends image to receipt endpoint
3. Celery worker processes OCR and parsing
4. API returns status and parsed fields
5. Frontend fills form automatically
6. User confirms and saves the transaction

